  "caveats": [
    "This is post-hoc after earlier baseline null results; small Monte Carlo p-values per serial swap-chain are descriptive and not pre-registered significance tests.",
    "Null preserves butterfly-host identities, native geography, plant family × continent × coarse climate stratum introduced range count per plant, and introduced plant richness per region and family.",
    "All 365 resource regions had previously sampled CHELSA BIO1/7/12/15 values, but region-level medians compress topographic and microclimatic heterogeneity.",
    "Randomization conserves introduced plant × region edges, not each butterfly's introduced-added resource count; climatic stratification alone does not condition on local habitat, introduction history, or sampling bias.",
    "The three climate stratification methods are not nested; don't interpret monotonic change across them as a causal share of climate explanation.",
    "Recorded resource geography does not measure butterfly abundance, host quality, local breeding, or competition.",
